# PROJECT: TUITION CENTER MANAGEMENT SYSTEM

Act as a senior full-stack software engineer, UI/UX designer, Firebase architect, database designer, accessibility specialist, and application security engineer.

Build a complete, production-oriented, mobile-first Tuition Center Management System.

Do not create only a landing page, dashboard mockup, or static prototype. Build the complete application foundation with all major pages, navigation, reusable components, forms, validation, role-aware interfaces, data models, service layers, error handling, loading states, security rules, and automated tests.

The system should be designed for a tuition center that typically manages approximately 100 active students. Students may remain enrolled for several months or several years. The application must preserve historical attendance and other required records for as long as they are retained under the center's policy. Do not implement automatic deletion of attendance after 60 days.

The application must be easy for a non-technical tuition administrator to operate, especially from a mobile phone.

Do not omit important features simply because the project is large. Implement the foundation in organized phases, preserve working functionality between phases, and clearly identify anything that requires manual configuration or an external service.

