10. ATTENDANCE MANAGEMENT
=========================

Attendance must be recorded per student per class session.

Supported states:

* NOT_MARKED
* PRESENT
* ABSENT
* LEFT

NOT_MARKED is a display state when no attendance document exists. It does not need to be stored as a document.

Use deterministic attendance document IDs:

attendance/{studentId}_{sessionId}

Each attendance document should contain:

* studentId
* batchId
* sessionId
* status
* arrivalAt
* departureAt
* arrivalClassification
* createdAt
* updatedAt
* recordedBy
* lastModifiedBy

ATTENDANCE RULES:

* Do not automatically mark students absent.
* An unmarked student must remain NOT_MARKED until the admin records attendance.
* PRESENT requires a valid arrival timestamp.
* ABSENT has no arrival or departure timestamp.
* LEFT is allowed only after the student has been marked PRESENT.
* Transitioning from PRESENT to LEFT must preserve the original arrival timestamp.
* LEFT must record a valid departure timestamp.
* The departure time must not be earlier than arrival time.
* Do not silently overwrite an existing attendance record.
* Do not create duplicate attendance records for the same student and session.
* Only the admin can record attendance.
* Parents have read-only access to attendance for their linked children.

ON-TIME/LATE CLASSIFICATION:

* Use the class session's scheduled start time and grace-period snapshot.
* Calculate the classification consistently.
* Make the grace period configurable by the admin.
* Store ON_TIME or LATE for PRESENT records.
* Use NOT_APPLICABLE for ABSENT records.
* Explain the exact comparison boundary used by the implementation.
* Prevent clients from arbitrarily changing the calculated classification without a permitted correction workflow.

Attendance corrections must use a controlled, audited admin workflow.

Do not implement attendance deletion as the normal correction method.

ATTENDANCE HISTORY:

* Provide date and batch filters.
* Provide student-specific history.
* Show arrival and departure times.
* Show attendance summaries and percentages.
* Clearly distinguish unmarked sessions from absences.
* Preserve attendance history for the configured retention period.
* Do not implement automatic 60-day deletion.

