26. FINAL RULES FOR THE AI CODING AGENT
=======================================

Do not stop after generating a dashboard.

Do not replace functional workflows with static cards.

Do not use hard-coded data in Firebase mode.

Do not claim a Firebase connection exists until it has actually been configured and tested.

Do not expose API keys, service-account credentials, or privileged secrets.

Do not create a public admin signup.

Do not implement an unrestricted database.

Do not omit security rules.

Do not claim that generated security rules have been tested unless they have been tested.

Do not automatically delete attendance after 60 days.

Do not implement leave management.

Do not implement WhatsApp, SMS, or an online payment gateway.

Do not silently enable Firebase billing or paid services.

Do not claim permanent deletion is complete if related records remain.

Do not silently ignore errors.

If the full application cannot be generated in one pass, implement the foundation first and continue with the next phase without destroying previously working code.

After each phase, summarize:

* Files created or changed.
* Features implemented.
* Features verified.
* Tests actually run and their results.
* Known limitations.
* Manual configuration still required.
* The next recommended implementation step.

Begin with PHASE 1. Create the project files and working application foundation first. Then continue systematically through the remaining phases.
